Please speak to your Google
Cloud sales representative

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:48.580
or your customer
engineer if you have

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.710
requirements for a
particular region that

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:54.090
is not shown over here.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:56.670
Google Cloud VMware
Engine is HIPAA compliant,

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.950
and other key industry
certifications

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.150
are being looked upon.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:04.970
These include ISO,
PCI DSS, and SOC.

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.890
Now, Google Cloud
VMware Engine truly

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:09.080
delivers a global
highly performant,

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:12.110
enterprise friendly, flexible
networking experience.

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:15.260
With simplified regional
and global routing modes,

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:18.320
you have one global
network with no necessity

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.560
to create regional network
designs and connect them.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.770
This greatly simplifies and
reduces the cost and complexity

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.770
to have more than one point
of presence in the Cloud.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:29.690
You can architect and
connect different parts

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:32.315
of your environment
easily across projects

00:14:32.315 --> 00:14:34.370
and across regions
with capabilities,

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:37.520
such as multi-VPC and
multi-region networking.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:41.150
With a fully redundant 100
Gbps east-west networking

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:45.110
with no oversubscription, as
well as a superior low latent

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.540
packet rate performance,
our architecture

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:50.240
really helps customers
who have applications

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.700
that are latency sensitive
or have high performance

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.550
networking requirements, such
as voice over IP applications,

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:58.430
and other end user workloads, as
you've heard from our customer

00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.600
testimony.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:01.940
Finally, with Google
Cloud VMware Engine,

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.830
your current networking
Windows solutions

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.450
can be brought to the Cloud.

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:09.050
We offer flexible public
ingress and egress options

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.630
with support for three
different ways for workloads

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:13.250
to get access to the internet.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.760
We have the Google Cloud VMware
Engine edge, the Google Cloud

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:19.190
edge, or your own corporate DNS.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.220
We also have built-in
integration with Cloud DNS,

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.070
and you can also bring
your own corporate DNS.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.930
We are an enterprise
ready platform

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:29.360
that scales and supports
for your enterprise

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.300
workloads with up to
64 node private clouds

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.430
running on highly
performant and scalable

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:37.580
Google Cloud infrastructure,
dynamic resource management

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.890
with autoscaling enabled.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.720
We also provide a
fully dedicated,

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:45.110
single-tenant high-performance
node with all NVMe storage

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:49.190
and with rich GCP networking,
and full functionality of NSX-T

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.940
with access to NSX-T manager.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:56.530
With 99.9 SLA in a single
zone with 5 to 32 nodes

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.750
in a cluster, you have
the high availability

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:02.830
that is required by some of your
mission critical applications.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:06.040
In addition, we also support
rich media environments

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:09.170
with large scale VMware Horizon
architectures supported,

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:13.300
as well as the ability to extend
and migrate VMware-based Citrix

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.530
media workloads.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.130
It's fully validated by Citrix.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.720
One of the questions
we often get

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.500
is, can I bring my VMware,
just my VMware environment,

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.120
or everything I consume on it.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.000
How can I make my VMware
environment and consumption

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.170
better in the Cloud?

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.920
The answer is we offer a fully
compatible VMware experience

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:35.430
so you can bring your existing
tools and processes as is.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.550
Whether it is your VMware Tools,
all your third party tools

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:42.240
that support VMware, as well as
our own marketplace services.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:44.590
In addition, you can take
advantage of Google Cloud

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:46.590
Services, whether
it is optimizing

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:50.190
the embedded protection using
Cloud Storage, a zero footprint

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.560
DR solution with
[INAUDIBLE],, building

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.570
hybrid, high performance,
and availability

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:58.170
architectures for databases,
modernizing your applications

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:02.040
using containers and Kubernetes,
centralizing and modernizing

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:05.310
your operations management,
or enriching your app's data

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.900
analytics, and more.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.460
In the next segment,
we will look

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.319
at a couple of these examples.

00:17:11.319 --> 00:17:13.540
Now, as you consume
VMware in the Cloud,

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:16.540
you want to ensure that you
avoid switching between screens

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.359
for operations management.

00:17:18.359 --> 00:17:20.470
For example, if you have
a performance problem,

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.928
you want to be able
to troubleshoot

00:17:21.928 --> 00:17:24.910
all aspects of the application
dependencies in one place

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.470
rather than go to
different systems

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.510
to solve part of the problem.

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.420
While the VMware Engine
service fully supports

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:34.780
existing VMware monitoring and
logging codes without changes,

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.720
as you start to develop more
hybrid applications that

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.750
actually live outside of
the VMware environment,

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:44.320
getting all operations data in
one place will be important.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:47.200
To solve this, you can use
Google Cloud's Operation

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.270
Service, formerly Stackdriver.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.580
You collect metrics,
logs, and places

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:55.780
across VMware Engine and
other Google Cloud Services.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:58.420
You can use built-in,
out-of-the-box dashboards

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.610
and views to monitor
your platform,

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:03.550
as well as the applications and
query and analyze these signals

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:04.600
as well.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.240
You can see the information
from the VMware infrastructure,

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.640
as well as the in-guest
and application.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.350
As far as the VMware
infrastructure goes,

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:13.720
you can see the vCenter,
the [INAUDIBLE] side

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.250
do log analysis.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.590
This does not require
any agent installation.

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:20.440
Metrics such as VM CPU,
disk, and network usage

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:22.051
are all available.

00:18:22.051 --> 00:18:23.670
For VM guests and
applications, you

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.280
can use open-source agents
to collect additional logs

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:26.930
and methods.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:29.490
So if you want to troubleshoot
any application or gain

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.860
insight into the
optimization or usage,

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:34.600
you can do it all in one place.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.040
As for the second
example, we will

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:38.830
look at a demo of how
we integrate BigQuery

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.590
with workloads running in
Google Cloud VMware Engine

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:45.316
to unlock the value of data
analytics for our customers.

